    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78199" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρα-κλῐδόν</span></b> , Adv., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακλίνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turning aside, swerving</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ
				ἂν ἔγωγε ἄλλα παρὲξ εἴποιμι π</span>. would not tell
			you another tale beside the mark and <i>swerving from the
			truth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.348
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσε π. ἔτραπεν
			ἄλλῃ</span> she turned her eyes <i>aside,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Ven.
				182
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πῖπτεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.757
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>leaning against</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοίχων ἔνθα καὶ
				ἔνθα π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				559
			</span></i>.</div>
